<title>UK: BP sets April LPG price at $172/$175 a tonne.</title>
<headline>BP sets April LPG price at $172/$175 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum announced on Thursday its April price for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG), the BP Agreed Price or BPAP.</p>
<p>The propane price will be $172 a tonne, down by $14 from the March level of $186 a tonne. And butane will be $175 a tonne, down by $30 from March's $205 a tonne. The price will be effective from April 1.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom,+44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
